                "source": "Twitter Web Client",
                "text": "September is Childhood Cancer Awareness Month. This month, we shine a light on the brave children fighting cancer, honor those we've lost, and support the families and medical teams standing beside them.  Only 4% of federal cancer research funding goes to childhood cancers \u2014 and that\u2019s not enough. Together, we can raise awareness, push for better treatments, and bring hope to the youngest fighters among us.  As Co-Chair of the Congressional Rare Disease Caucus, I\u2019m fighting for reauthorization of the Pediatric Disease Priority Review Voucher \u2013 a program with proven results to create cures for pediatric cancer.  I urge my colleagues to join me in this fight. Let\u2019s turn awareness into action.    #ChildhoodCancerAwareness #FightLikeAKid #HopeForKids",
